{"ratings":[{"id":"C1","consequence":"secret","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A size cut through a JSON-escaped credential can leave part of it in stored output and text sent to models."},{"id":"C2","consequence":"secret","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Dropping a blank line prevents a multiline credential from matching, exposing its private lines in failure excerpts."},{"id":"C3","consequence":"outage","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A gate emitting many very long lines can exhaust daemon memory because retained diagnostic lines have no byte bound."},{"id":"C4","consequence":"secret","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Redacting an overlapping shorter credential first can expose the remaining lines of a multiline credential in failure excerpts."},{"id":"C5","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A field containing the redaction marker is withheld in full, potentially hiding diagnostics needed to resolve a failed run."},{"id":"C7","consequence":"state","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Loading and saving a run can permanently remove literal terminal escape sequences from persisted instructions."},{"id":"C8","consequence":"nuisance","trigger":"normal","reason":"The endpoint serves compact JSON, but the UI parses it and renders or pretty-prints it for display."}]}